  "gaps": [
    "The student's chosen concentration is not known; the 21-hour concentration block is recorded as a single requirement. Course lists: General (select 7 of 21 listed courses), Emergency and Disaster Management (EDMG220, EDMG230, PBHE413, PBHE426, EDMG340, EDMG420, PSYC431), Nutrition and Wellness (SOCI315, SPHE340, SPHE314, SOCI423, SPHE460, SPHE461, SPHE470), Public Health Informatics (HIMA100, HIMA110, HIMA250, HIMA310, HIMA360, HIMA410, HIMA460).",
    "Capture does not state any residency or institutional-credit requirement (minimum credits that must be completed at the school), nor whether the capstone must be completed at the school.",
    "Capture does not state minimum grade or GPA requirements, transfer credit limits, or upper-division credit minimums.",
    "Footnote markers ('1' after Arts & Humanities, '2' after PBHE498) appear detached from their text; the footnotes appear to be: literature courses require ENGL101 or ENGL110, and PBHE498 requires senior standing, completion of all major courses, and must be taken as the last course before graduation. The mapping is inferred from order, not explicitly linked in the capture."
  ],
